# Exchange workflow contract

schema: colab-exchange-workflow-contract/1
status: builder contract for 0511.workflow-colab/05.03. Not shared-interface law. Not a release.
keeps: labs/colab-workflow-pass01 and its 05.02 contract. That tool stays the v1 workflow.

## Scope
labs/colab-workflow-pass02 opens one caller-selected investigation in space 0, pages 0701–0799. The door 0700.band.colabs is not a member. The live book D:\Git\lib-build\00.kernel\00.00.10.work is refused as the book. The tool does not prepare a package, call a model, reserve, capture, allocate a member, or write 00.live.

The fact store is investigation.json, schema colab-exchange-investigation/1. There is no status field and no derived flag stored. seal.json is the last file of a finished write. A missing seal, .write.lock, or partial.json means resume refused. The tool does not delete retained files.

## Pins, checked before launch
- Producer labs/colab-support-pass02/colab_support.py sha256 2b720434ac4c4331835c1484b0eca362e01e8afbecde0ab800ca392530abf68b, 53892 bytes.
- Producer v1 sha256 33bbe41c52485fc7b2b611d830bae8a15129721ad807a931e8193f17944c467c, 67781 bytes. The v2 producer loads it. This workflow does not edit it.
- Assembler sha256 75d49679cbf3e624a82573229ca8c7cd9b758799bc26b6f080111feb6eaa275c, 43928 bytes.
- Checker sha256 9bbd9d57f3b7da43234ac2e6ae4ce40a0ab6af2f53c8135ecfb2ee0c8a6e322d, 21563 bytes.
- Helper sha256 8f3da5c651f6924fca6dedb0b95da7d181eb58884dc030dd9cbc3d8b6a5b15ac, 45767 bytes.
- Inspector sha256 947915febaa5918f56b6be03c81840c030d081fcab9a3bead2cd660973a9999b, 11402 bytes.

A mismatch refuses with pin mismatch and does not launch. The process interpreter runs `python -B` with an argument array and no shell. The command is `colab_support.py verify`. handoff_check.py is not invoked. `--config` is local colab-config/2. Its absolute paths are not copied into the investigation, the provenance file, or any projection.

## Names
For pass 05.NN the page files are 05.NN.pack.md, 05.NN.return.md, 06.NN.notes.md, and 06.NN.review.md. Binding pass remains 05.NN. 08.md is the pointer projection. It is not a fifth exchange body.

Source paths may name a directory ending in .colab and a file named 07.md. Emitted workflow names may not. The tool does not create 07.md and does not emit a name ending in .colab.

## Open
`open --request ABS --closure ABS` reads package/source-manifest.json and package/<snapshot>. The binding investigation book, page, and pass, and the binding targets, must equal the open request. A difference is wrong origin.

`open --request ABS --sources ABS` reads a caller tree at source.path. The open request is schema colab-exchange-open/1. Kind id refuses unsupported section id. A heading counts only outside a fence, and only as the exact line. Occurrence null requires one match. An integer occurrence is 1-based.

Open does not write a return or a review.

## Attach
```text
python -B colab_workflow.py attach --book ABS --page PAGE --pass 05.NN --output ABS --config ABS --expect-digest HEX [--producer ABS]
```

`--output` is the producer output root. Order: refuse a partial page, refuse a link, pin, launch verify, then require command result intact and digest equal to `--expect-digest`. The recorded verification.json schema must be colab-package-verification/2 and its digest must equal that same value. Its investigation must equal the open page. Package file hashes must equal verification.json. An intact verify whose digest differs is stale expected hash. A missing verification.json is malformed package. Any other verify failure is conflicting bytes.

Under artifacts/05.NN/ the tool keeps package/, prepared-colab.zip, verification.json, and provenance.json schema colab-exchange-provenance/1. It does not keep evaluator/, assembler-request.json, assembler-run.json, assembler-output/, or handoff.json. It does not store the verifier stdout.

05.NN.pack.md is the exact package pack bytes. The preparation notes stay byte for byte under the artifacts. 06.NN.notes.md is a projection: a header, then exactly launch-bytes of the snapshot, then a working section. `append-note` adds one supplied line to that working section. The same line again is a readonly repeat. The snapshot hash and the package digest stay the same.

The same digest and the same kept bytes are a readonly repeat. Other bytes on that pass are conflicting bytes.

## Return
`place-return` pins the helper and the inspector, inspects the named member, and runs `return_capture.py verify`. Status must be complete. Origin book, page, and batch must equal the investigation book, page, and pass. The return.md bytes must match the capture hash and length. Those bytes are written as 05.NN.return.md with nothing added. The member, receipt sha256, and return sha256 are stored on the pass and rendered in 08.md.

A missing or incomplete member is partial custody. A different origin is wrong origin. A hash that does not match the receipt record is hash conflict. The same bytes are a readonly repeat. Different bytes on an occupied pass refuse and leave the placed bytes in place. The tool does not allocate another member.

## Review
`record-review` requires a placed return. The input is schema colab-exchange-review/1. It supplies the assessment, each finding's disposition, reason, source binding, and director reply, the pending questions, and one route: hold, finish, request-next, or route-n5nn. A missing director reply refuses. The strings pending and not needed are accepted only when the caller supplies them. source binding must name a target on the investigation. request-next requires an explicit next pass and writes no pack for it. finish with an unresolved finding refuses. Unresolved findings are listed in 06.NN.review.md. A route is not approval. The same record is a readonly repeat. A different record on an occupied pass refuses and leaves the review in place.

## Limits
Space 0 only. One repository and one commit, because that is the accepted producer limit. No face 07. No live investigation. No app command and no edit of 00.live. The digest is not inside the ZIP. The caller passes `--expect-digest`. A verified package is not approval. Returned text and Director words are data.
